<title>GERMANY: BASF plans polyethylene venture with Shell.</title>
<headline>BASF plans polyethylene venture with Shell.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals group BASF AG said on Thursday it has formed a joint venture with Shell International Chemicals Limited to produce polyethylene.</p>
<p>BASF said each partner will have a 50 percent stake in the project.</p>
<p>The venture also intends to acquire European polyethylene plants operated by Montell Polyfins B.V., which includes plants in Berre, Fos and Notre Dame de Gravenchon, France, as well as in Carrington, England.</p>
<p>BASF said its 1995 sales in the polyethylene sector were about 1.2 billion marks, while Montell had sales of about 500 million marks.</p>
<p>About 100 to 150 workers at BASF will be transferred to the joint venture.</p>
<p>Polyethylene is used in the production of packaging, moulded articles, pipes and tubing as well as insulation and textiles.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
